73 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (Text file savegame.txt: marker CS211_2048_V1, then score and moves, then 5 rows of 5 integers. load_game checks the marker, two nonnegative int counters, exactly 25 cells that are 0 or powers of two \(at least 2\), int range, and no extra content. It fills temporaries and copies into the game only after the whole file passes.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
74 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (Reads one line per command \(w a s d, v save, o load, n new game with y/n confirmation, h help, e exit\), rejects anything else, and exits cleanly on end of input. On a changed move it adds the points, counts one move, inserts one 2, redisplays, and announces a win when the highest tile first reaches 2048 or more. Play continues after a win; at game over only v, o, n, h and e work.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
