/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 47 0 R
/T (Final check: the sum is 50 and 50 % 10 = 0, so the sum is divisible by 10 and the number passes the Luhn checksum. The check digit is chosen so the whole sum lands on a multiple of 10, so a single wrong digit moves the sum off a multiple of 10 and is caught. Contrast: changing the last digit to 7 \(4532015112830367\) raises the first term from 6 to 7, giving a sum of 51; 51 % 10 = 1, so it fails. The program prints the same sums \(50 and 51\).)
/E (Final check: the sum is 50 and 50 % 10 = 0, so the sum is divisible by 10 and the number passes the Luhn checksum. The check digit is chosen so the whole sum lands on a multiple of 10, so a single wrong digit moves the sum off a multiple of 10 and is caught. Contrast: changing the last digit to 7 \(4532015112830367\) raises the first term from 6 to 7, giving a sum of 51; 51 % 10 = 1, so it fails. The program prints the same sums \(50 and 51\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
