379 0 obj
<<
/Title (Traversal order: right to left. The rightmost digit is left unchanged, and every second digit moving left is doubled. A doubled value above 9 has 9 subtracted \(equivalent to adding its two digits\). All resulting values are added.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 335 0 R
/First 423 0 R
/Last 424 0 R
/Count -7
/Next 380 0 R
>>
endobj
380 0 obj
<<
/Title (Final check: the sum is 50 and 50 % 10 = 0, so the sum is divisible by 10 and the number passes the Luhn checksum. The check digit is chosen so the whole sum lands on a multiple of 10, so a single wrong digit moves the sum off a multiple of 10 and is caught. Contrast: changing the last digit to 7 \(4532015112830367\) raises the first term from 6 to 7, giving a sum of 51; 51 % 10 = 1, so it fails. The program prints the same sums \(50 and 51\).)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 335 0 R
/Prev 379 0 R
>>
endobj
